<title>JAPAN: Japan 4-year note auction lowest price of 100.04.</title>
<headline>Japan 4-year note auction lowest price of 100.04.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The auction of 400 billion yen worth of 1.4 percent four-year government notes produced the following results, the Ministry of Finance said on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 100.04    Stop rate	   1.389 pct</p>
<p>Average price	100.07    Average yield     1.380 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   1.2874 trillion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	399.3 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 40.9867 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    Aug 20, 1997   Maturity    Aug 20, 2001</p>
<p>Coupon payment     Feb 20, Aug 20</p>
</text>
